\section{Where the state lives}

Quota state goes in the \emph{data} directory
(\cref{sec:enrichment-cache} established the [[SCHOLAR_DATA_DIR]]
convention), not the cache directory---and the distinction is
load-bearing.
[[scholar cache clear]] is the documented remedy for stale search
results, and a user whose IEEE searches return nothing will reach for it.
If clearing the cache also erased the memory that today's 200 requests
are spent, the remedy would un-block the provider locally while it is
still blocked remotely, and the next search would burn requests just to
rediscover the block.
We reuse [[notes.get_data_dir]] rather than re-deriving the path so all
data-directory consumers stay in agreement.

One file per quota group (rather than one file for all providers) keeps
two concurrent [[scholar]] processes that hit \emph{different} providers
off each other's files entirely; the concurrency story for the same
provider is discussed with [[save_state]] below.

<<state functions>>=
def get_state_dir() -> Path:
    """Return the directory holding rate-limit state files.

    The directory is created if it does not exist.  It lives under the
    data directory (`SCHOLAR_DATA_DIR`), not the cache directory, so
    `scholar cache clear` does not erase quota bookkeeping.
    """
    path = get_data_dir() / STATE_DIR_NAME
    path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    return path


def _state_file(name: str) -> Path:
    return get_state_dir() / f"{name}.json"
<<constants>>=
STATE_DIR_NAME = "rate_limits"
@

