\subsection{Recording limit hits}
\label{sec:ratelimit-record-limit-hit}

Some limit signals never pass through [[record_response]]---client
libraries like [[pyalex]] raise instead of returning responses, and
IEEE's quota rejection is a 403 whose meaning only the IEEE provider can
decode.
[[record_limit_hit]] is the direct entry point for those cases.

The [[exhausted_daily]] flag is the self-correction half of the daily
reset guess (\cref{sec:ratelimit-time}): when the provider explicitly
says the daily quota is spent, we force the day count to the declared
limit \emph{and} set a cooldown to the next reset.
This is what makes an undercounted tally (the accepted concurrency race)
or a wrongly guessed reset time cost at most one request: the first
rejection re-establishes the truth.

<<rate limiter methods>>=
def record_limit_hit(self, *, retry_after: float | None = None,
                     until: float | None = None, reason: str = "",
                     exhausted_daily: bool = False) -> None:
    """Persist a rate-limit or quota rejection.

    `retry_after` is a delay in seconds, `until` an absolute epoch
    timestamp; with neither, a default cooldown applies.  Set
    `exhausted_daily` when the provider signalled that the daily quota
    is spent: the day count is forced to the declared limit and the
    cooldown extends to the next daily reset.
    """
    state = load_state(self.name)
    if exhausted_daily:
        if self.limits.daily:
            state["day_count"] = max(
                state["day_count"], self.limits.daily
            )
            state["daily_limit"] = self.limits.daily
        if until is None and retry_after is None:
            until = next_daily_reset()
    if until is None:
        delay = (
            retry_after if retry_after is not None else DEFAULT_COOLDOWN
        )
        until = _now() + delay
    state["cooldown_until"] = until
    state["cooldown_reason"] = reason or "rate limited"
    state["cooldown_quota"] = exhausted_daily
    save_state(self.name, state)
<<constants>>=
# Cooldown applied on a 429 without a usable Retry-After, in seconds.
DEFAULT_COOLDOWN = 60.0
@

